          "en": ["Bring 500 ml of the milk to a boil, split it with the diluted lemon juice, strain through muslin and rinse well with water. Keep this chhena aside (do not squeeze completely dry).", "Boil the remaining 1.5 litres of milk in a wide, heavy kadai and simmer on medium heat, stirring often, for 30–35 minutes until it reduces to about a third and looks thick.", "Add the chhena and cook, stirring, for 8–10 minutes until the mixture is thick and grainy. Add the sugar — it will loosen — and keep cooking until it starts leaving the sides of the pan.", "Stir in the cardamom and saffron and spread the mixture about 2 cm thick in a greased tray. Smooth the top and sprinkle with pistachios and rose petals.", "Let it set at room temperature for 3–4 hours (or chill 2 hours), then cut into 12 squares."],
